# a-base-that-plays-its-list — plan 16 W4, the whole plan in one run.
#
# The first scenario in the suite where nothing outside the simulation
# says when a wave arrives.  The script arms a list, the player drives
# out and pokes a spawn marker eighteen hexes from home, and from that
# point the base plays on its own: wave 1 stands its five seconds, walks
# in, is fought, and wave 2 follows a lull later with no line here
# asking for it.
#
# ⚠ **This is what plan 15 C3 was waiting for.**  Every clock plans 12,
# 13, 14 and 15 measured was measured during wave 1, on a base that
# ended when the first wave got in.  `tests/16_w4_the_real_length.loft`
# is the measurement; this file is the game-level record that it is a
# game and not a fixture.
#
# ⚠ The trip out is the trigger's price, and it is not decoration: the
# player is eighteen hexes from the core at the moment the wave stands
# up, and has to drive home in front of it.

echo a base that plays its list: poked once, then it runs on its own

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
click 1 0
click 1 2
click 1 -2
marker 1 0 tower
marker 1 2 tower

do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 18 0
marker 18 0 spawn 3

count markers 5 5
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 20 -2
drag -3 -1 20 -1
drag -3 0 20 0
drag -3 1 20 1
drag -3 2 20 2
count painted 120 120

# The wall, with (6, 0) left open — the gate a crew member can plug.
palette 9
click 6 -2
click 6 -1
click 6 1
click 6 2
kind 6 0 grass
kind 6 1 wall

crew 6 0
helper 0 6 0
roster 1 1
park 0 0

# The mission's list, armed.  Nothing has poked it.
schedule 12 12 12 12
waves 0 0
count alive 0 0

# ── The poke ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
drive 18 0
tick 10
vehicle 18 0
waves 1 1
count alive 12 12

# ── The drive home, in front of them ────────────────────────────
drive 0 0
tick 10
vehicle 0 0

# ── And the base plays on, and SURVIVES ─────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ No line here asks for wave 2.  It arrives because wave 1 was
# cleared and the lull ran out — and so do waves 3 and 4.
#
# ⚠⚠ **The player parked at the core is doing UPKEEP** (plan 17 T1).
# The tower at (1, 0) is one hex away, which is inside its own
# footprint, so every time it goes black the player rebuilds it over
# 20 s — no key pressed, because repair is a POSITION.  Before T1 this
# same file measured a base that fell at 256 having played two waves.
tick 500
waves 4 4
count alive 0 0

# Still standing, with points left — the first scenario in the suite
# where a base outlives its own wave list.
wallet 20.0 80.0

# The gate blocker was lost holding it, and nobody went back.
roster 0 0
cargo 1 1

snap w4_a_base_that_plays_its_list
